{
  "$schema": "../../scenario.schema.json",
  "id": "orchestration/a-loop-s-parallel-review-that-raises-fails-at-once-and-cuts-the-other-reviews",
  "title": "A Loop whose parallel reviewers review an output, one of whose reviews raises (its reviewer left the kit), fails the loop with that error without waiting for the other reviews: each of them has started, posted pending, and is cut, posted failed 'cancelled'",
  "rules": [
    "§19.7.4"
  ],
  "notes": "Python: orchestration/strategies/loop.py _review_parallel (core/task_utils.py gather_or_cut: the first error cuts the others, then is raised); tests/orchestration/test_loop_strategy.py TestReviewParallel::test_the_first_error_cuts_the_other_reviewers. Decided by the maintainer, HITL 4080f241 (RMK-1279). The raising reviewer is the first: each review still starts, posted pending, before the error answers; the slow reviewer's model holds at a gate never opened, so whether its turn reached the model is not pinned.",
  "setup": {
    "channels": [
      {
        "id": "sms",
        "type": "sms",
        "category": "transport"
      },
      {
        "id": "writer",
        "type": "ai",
        "agent": {},
        "model": {
          "rounds": [
            {
              "text": "Draft one."
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "slow",
        "type": "ai",
        "agent": {
          "role": "Slow"
        },
        "model": {
          "rounds": [
            {
              "text": "APPROVED",
              "gate": "slow"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "gone",
        "type": "ai",
        "agent": {
          "role": "Gone"
        },
        "model": {
          "rounds": [
            {
              "text": "APPROVED"
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    ],
    "rooms": [
      {
        "id": "r1",
        "bindings": [
          {
            "channel_id": "sms"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "strategies": [
      {
        "id": "loop",
        "loop": {
          "agent": "writer",
          "reviewers": [
            "gone",
            "slow"
          ],
          "strategy": "parallel"
        }
      }
    ],
    "hooks": [
      {
        "name": "errors",
        "trigger": "on_error",
        "execution": "async"
      }
    ]
  },
  "steps": [
    {
      "call": "install_strategy",
      "room_id": "r1",
      "strategy": "loop"
    },
    {
      "call": "unregister_channel",
      "channel_id": "gone"
    },
    {
      "call": "process_inbound",
      "room_id": "r1",
      "message": {
        "channel_id": "sms",
        "sender_id": "u1",
        "content": {
          "type": "text",
          "body": "Write it."
        }
      },
      "expect": {
        "result": {
          "blocked": false,
          "error": {
            "$present": true
          }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "idle": true
    },
    {
      "call": "status.recent",
      "agent_id": "slow",
      "expect": {
        "result": [
          {
            "agent_id": "slow",
            "action": "review",
            "status": "pending",
            "metadata": {
              "room_id": "r1",
              "strategy": "parallel",
              "task_run": true
            }
          },
          {
            "agent_id": "slow",
            "action": "review",
            "status": "failed",
            "detail": "cancelled",
            "metadata": {
              "room_id": "r1",
              "strategy": "parallel",
              "task_run": true
            }
          }
        ]
      }
    }
  ],
  "expect": {
    "timeline": {
      "r1": [
        {
          "source": {
            "channel_id": "sms"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    "models": {
      "writer": [
        {
          "messages": [
            {
              "role": "user",
              "text": "Write it."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "gone": []
    },
    "hooks": {
      "errors": [
        {
          "trigger": "on_error",
          "room_id": "r1",
          "event": {
            "source": {
              "channel_id": "writer"
            },
            "chain_depth": 1,
            "responds_to": "r1#0",
            "metadata": {
              "error_category": "generation"
            }
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  }
}
